course: dictionary
lesson: 12927
title: Evaluation: judging and working things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An evaluation is a careful judgement of how good, useful or valuable something is. When you evaluate something, you ask: what went well, what went wrong, and how could it be better?
explain: «The class wrote an evaluation of their science experiment.» Here the pupils judged the experiment. They thought about what worked and what did not. The verb is evaluate, and the noun is evaluation.
explain: Evaluation can also mean a written or spoken report that gives that judgement. «Our teacher gave us a clear evaluation of our project.» Here the evaluation is the report itself.
explain: In maths, evaluation means working out the value of an expression. «Evaluate 3 × (2 + 4).» Do the bracket first: 2 + 4 = 6, then 3 × 6 = 18. So the answer is 18.
fact: Evaluation means careful judging of how good, useful or valuable something is.
fact: An evaluation can also be a written or spoken report that gives that judgement.
fact: In science, the evaluation section asks what went well, what went wrong and how to improve.
fact: In maths, to evaluate an expression means to work out its value: evaluate 3 × (2 + 4) = 18.
fact: «Self-evaluation» means judging your own work.
exercise: «The class wrote an evaluation of their science experiment.» What does evaluation mean here? | A type of experiment with bright lights | *A careful judgement of what went well and what went wrong | A party to celebrate the end of term | A new science book
exercise: «Our teacher gave us an evaluation of our project.» What is the evaluation? | A long walk around the school | A list of spelling words | A prize for the best drawing | *A report that judges how good the project is
exercise: Evaluate 3 × (2 + 4). What is the answer? | 6 | *18 | 24 | 9
test: «In design and technology, we must evaluate our products.» What does evaluate mean? | Paint the classroom | *Judge how good and useful our product is | Make a cake | Count how many pieces we have
test: What does self-evaluation mean? | Asking a friend to write your homework | *Judging how good your own work is | Evaluating someone else's maths | Painting a picture of yourself
exam: Which sentence uses evaluation as a maths word? | *Evaluate 5 × (1 + 3) to find its value | The science evaluation was printed out | The teacher wrote an evaluation of the story | Her evaluation was kind and fair
